metadata:
  name: Parmigiano di Melanzane 
  images:
    - https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Melanzane_alla_parmigiana_finished.jpg/960px-Melanzane_alla_parmigiana_finished.jpg
  description: From https://www.insidetherustickitchen.com/parmigiana-di-melanzane-aubergine-parmigana/ 
  types: [Main]
  estimatedPrepTime: 2 h
  servings: 4 people

ingredients:
 - 2 st large aubergines/eggplant, around (700g/ 1.5 lbs)
 - 700 g pureed tomatoes (passata), chunky or smooth texture
 - 1 st white onion
 - 1 st bunch of basil
 - 250 g mozzarella cheese, cut into cubes
 - 0.75 cups Parmigiano Reggiano cheese, freshly grated (70g)
 - 0.5 tbsp olive oil
 - 1 dl flour, for dusting
 - 1 dl sunflower oil, for frying (around 1/2 cup/125ml)
 - 1 st salt and pepper, to season

actions:
 - free_text Thinly slice the 2 large aubergines (around 700 g) then place them in a colander. Sprinkle them lightly with salt and set them aside for 1 hour. This drains off any excess water and helps with frying.
 - free_text Meanwhile, make the simple tomato sauce. Finely chop 1 white onion and sauté in a pan with 0.5 tbsp olive oil until translucent and soft but not browned. Add 700 g tomato passata (pureed tomatoes) and 1 small bunch of basil torn with your hands. Add a pinch of salt and pepper, stir then let it simmer gently for 10-15 minutes. Set aside.
 - free_text Rinse the eggplant slices under cold water and pat them dry with a kitchen towel or paper. Lightly dust them with 1 dl flour, shaking off any excess then fry them in 1 dl sunflower oil for a few seconds each side, drain on kitchen paper to remove any excess oil.
 - free_text Preheat the oven to 180°C/350F/gas mark 4. I used an 11×8 inch oval dish but a rectangle or square dish around the same size will work too e.g 10×8 inch.
 - free_text Spoon a small amount of tomato sauce into the bottom of a baking dish and spread it around, this will stop the eggplant from sticking.
 - free_text Next add one layer of eggplant to the dish followed by a sprinkling of the 0.75 cups grated Parmigiano Reggiano, cubes of the 250 g mozzarella, a sprinkling of pepper and couple spoons of tomato sauce (save 1/3 of the sauce for the final layer). Continue with the next layer until you have one top layer left.
 - free_text For the top layer, spoon over the remaining tomato sauce and top with parmesan and mozzarella. Cover loosely with foil and bake for 20 minutes, remove the foil and bake for another 20 minutes until nice and golden and bubbling on top. Let it rest for 5 minutes before serving.
